course: dictionary
lesson: 14167
title: Changing old things to be new
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Modernised» means made modern. Something is modernised when it is changed with new equipment, methods or ideas so that it is up to date. «A modernised kitchen» has new cookers and cupboards.
explain: «Modernised» is the past form of the verb «modernise». The verb has four forms: modernise, modernises, modernised and modernising. «They modernised the old school» tells you the school was changed in the past.
explain: Look at the words around it to help you. If a sentence talks about old buildings, trains or kitchens, the word «modernised» probably means they were updated. In history, countries such as Japan modernised with railways, factories and schools.
explain: The spelling changes slightly by country. British English writes «modernised», and American English writes «modernized». Both mean the same thing.
fact: «Modernised» means made modern and up to date.
fact: «Modernise» is the verb, and «modernised» is its past form.
fact: Things can be modernised by adding new equipment, new methods or new ideas.
fact: «Updated» is a close synonym for «modernised».
fact: Countries such as Japan modernised in the 1800s with railways, factories and schools.
exercise: «The town modernised its old railway station.» What does modernised mean? | Painted in old colours | *Changed with new equipment so it is up to date | Knocked down to the ground | Made smaller and quieter
exercise: Which word is the past form of modernise? | *modernised | modern | modernise | modernising
exercise: «In history, Japan modernised with railways and factories after 1868.» What does modernised suggest here? | *Changed to use new railways, factories and schools | Turned into a museum | Stopped building anything | Went back to old ways
test: «The bus station was modernised last month.» Which word is the best swap for modernised? | Glum | Abandoned | Ancient | *Updated
test: «A newly modernised station» has what kind of equipment? | No equipment at all | *New, up-to-date equipment | Equipment from long ago | Old, broken equipment
exam: «The old factory was modernised with new machines.» What does the sentence tell you? | The factory is still very old | The machines were given away | The factory was knocked down | *The factory was updated with new machines
